-- database engine
Cluster
-- SHOW CREATE DATABASE prints the engine with the cluster name
1
-- SHOW TABLES lists the tables of the database on the cluster
t
-- each table is exposed as a Distributed storage
Distributed
-- SHOW CREATE TABLE prints a Distributed table over the named cluster
1
-- DESCRIBE reflects the remote structure
id	UInt64
s	String
-- SELECT is forwarded to the cluster
1	a
2	b
3	c
-- INSERT is forwarded to the cluster
1	a
2	b
3	c
4	d
-- EXISTS TABLE for an existing and a missing table
1
0
-- a SELECT from a missing table reports UNKNOWN_TABLE and must not recurse into the name hints
1
-- the cluster name may come from a macro, like in the Distributed table engine
4
-- a multi-shard database reads from every shard and accepts INSERT queries by default
8
5
-- the implicit sharding key of a multi-shard database is included in SHOW CREATE TABLE
1
-- SHOW CREATE TABLE preserves column defaults, aliases and materialized expressions
ALIAS a + 2
DEFAULT a + 1
MATERIALIZED a + 3
-- an unknown cluster is rejected at CREATE (prints 1 if the expected error is raised)
1
-- a wrong number of arguments is rejected (prints 1 if the expected error is raised)
1
-- a database that refers to itself is rejected instead of recursing (prints 1 if the expected error is raised)
1
1
-- a cycle through a Remote database terminates instead of recursing
1
1
-- a shard that is unavailable fails the SELECT with the real error, while the metadata is served by the available shard
t
1
-- DDL against a Cluster database is not supported (prints 1 if the expected error is raised)
1
1
1
5
